To analyze WPA2 wireless security and capture a handshake, follow these steps:
Set up your wireless interface to monitor mode using airmon-ng start wlan0 to listen to all Wi-Fi traffic.
Identify the target network by scanning for nearby access points with airdump-ng wlan0mon and capturing the handshake.
Capture the handshake using airdump-ng -c [channel] --bssid [target BSSID] -w [file] wlan0mon.
Verify the capture by checking the presence of the 4-way handshake in the captured file.
Perform dictionary attacks on the captured handshake to crack the password, using tools like aircrack-ng or hashcat.
